{
  "id": "L27-recent-cache",
  "level": 27,
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "use": "practice",
  "status": "ready",
  "order": 1,
  "title": "Recent Cache",
  "statement": "A server keeps a cache of at most capacity entries. Each operation is a string: \"put key value\" or \"get key\". A get returns the value for the key, or −1 if it is missing, and counts as a use. A put stores or updates the key and counts as a use; if the cache is then over capacity, the least recently used key is removed. Return the results of the get operations in order.",
  "examples": [
    {
      "input": "capacity = 2, ops = [\"put 1 1\", \"put 2 2\", \"get 1\", \"put 3 3\", \"get 2\", \"get 3\"]",
      "output": "[1, -1, 3]"
    },
    {
      "input": "capacity = 1, ops = [\"put 5 7\", \"put 5 8\", \"get 5\"]",
      "output": "[8]"
    }
  ],
  "constraints": [
    "1 <= capacity <= 1000",
    "1 <= ops.length <= 10^4",
    "1 <= key <= 10^4, 0 <= value <= 10^4"
  ],
  "answerKey": {
    "pattern": "A hash map plus an ordering of keys by last use (a linked list, or an ordered map)",
    "keyPoints": [
      "Every use moves the key to the most recent end",
      "On overflow, remove the key at the least recent end",
      "Map from key to its node gives O(1) moves"
    ],
    "timeComplexity": "O(1) per operation",
    "spaceComplexity": "O(capacity)",
    "edgeCases": [
      "Updating an existing key also refreshes it",
      "Capacity 1",
      "get of a missing key"
    ],
    "acceptableSlowerApproaches": [
      "Keep a list and search it on every use: O(capacity) per operation"
    ]
  },
  "hints": [
    "What two things must be fast: finding a key, and finding the oldest key?",
    "A hash map finds keys; a doubly linked list (or an insertion-ordered map) keeps the order of use.",
    "On each use, unlink the key and append it at the newest end; evict from the oldest end."
  ],
  "starterCode": {
    "javascript": "function recentCache(capacity, ops) {\n  // return the results of the get operations\n}",
    "java": "class Solution {\n  int[] recentCache(int capacity, String[] ops) {\n    // return the results of the get operations\n  }\n}"
  },
  "similarLeetCode": "LRU Cache",
